                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                XTENSION= 'BINTABLE'           /Written by IDL:  Tue Mar  1 15:26:07 2022       BITPIX  =                    8 /                                                NAXIS   =                    2 /Binary table                                    NAXIS1  =                   72 /Number of bytes per row                         NAXIS2  =                  448 /Number of rows                                  PCOUNT  =                    0 /Random parameter count                          GCOUNT  =                    1 /Group count                                     TFIELDS =                   10 /Number of columns                               EXTNAME = 'CLOCK_CORRECT'      /Swift Clock Correction                          DATE    = '2022-03-01'         /Creation date                                   TFORM1  = '1D      '           /Real*8 (double precision)                       TTYPE1  = 'TSTART  '           /Label for column 1                              TUNIT1  = 's       '           /Units of column 1                               TFORM2  = '1D      '           /Real*8 (double precision)                       TTYPE2  = 'TSTOP   '           /Label for column 2                              TUNIT2  = 's       '           /Units of column 2                               TFORM3  = '1D      '           /Real*8 (double precision)                       TTYPE3  = 'TOFFSET '           /Label for column 3                              TUNIT3  = 's       '           /Units of column 3                               TFORM4  = '1D      '           /Real*8 (double precision)                       TTYPE4  = 'C0      '           /Label for column 4                              TFORM5  = '1D      '           /Real*8 (double precision)                       TTYPE5  = 'C1      '           /Label for column 5                              TFORM6  = '1D      '           /Real*8 (double precision)                       TTYPE6  = 'C2      '           /Label for column 6                              TFORM7  = '1D      '           /Real*8 (double precision)                       TTYPE7  = 'MAXGAP  '           /Label for column 7                              TUNIT7  = 'd       '           /Units of column 7                               TFORM8  = '1J      '           /Integer*4 (long integer)                        TTYPE8  = 'TYPE    '           /Label for column 8                              TFORM9  = '1D      '           /Real*8 (double precision)                       TTYPE9  = 'CHI_N   '           /Label for column 9                              TFORM10 = '1J      '           /Integer*4 (long integer)                        TTYPE10 = 'DOF     '           /Label for column 10                             ORIGIN  = 'NASA/GSFC'          /Source of FITS file                             CREATOR = 'IDL     '           /Creator                                         VERSION =                  147 /Extension version number                        FILENAME= 'swclockcor20041120v147.fits' /File name                              CONTENT = 'CLOCK_CORRECTIONS'  /Clock corrections                               TIMEUNIT= 's       '           /Units of header time keywords                   MJDREFI =                51910 /2001.0(UTC) expressed in TT (int)               MJDREFF =    0.000742870370000 /2001.0(UTC) expressed in TT (fract)             TSTART  =        122671814.583 /Start time (raw spacecraft)                     TSTOP   =        667825216.992 /Stop time (raw spacecraft)                      DATE-OBS= '2004-11-20T19:30:14' /Start time (UTC)                               DATE-END= '2022-03-01T11:00:11' /Stop time (UTC)                                TELESCOP= 'SWIFT   '           /Telescope (mission) name                        INSTRUME= 'SC      '           /Instrument name                                 CCLS0001= 'BCF     '           /Dataset is a Basic Calibration File             CCNM0001= 'CLOCK   '           /Type of calibration data                        CDES0001= 'SPACECRAFT CLOCK OFFSET FILE' /Description                           CDTP0001= 'DATA    '           /Calibration file contains data                  CVSD0001= '2004-11-20'         /UTC date when calibration should first be used  CVST0001= '19:30:14'           /UTC time when calibration should first be used  COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT  Swift clock correction file                                            COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT  This file is used by tools that correct Swift times for the measured   COMMENT  offset of the spacecraft clock based on fits to data provided by the   COMMENT  Swift MOC. The columns contain polynomial coefficients for various timeCOMMENT  ranges and are used to compute the appropriate clock correction for anyCOMMENT  given mission elapsed time (after the first post-launch measurement).  COMMENT  The technique is very similar to that used for RXTE fine timing.       COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT  In contrast to RXTE where these fine clock corrections have magnitudes COMMENT  measured in the tens of microseconds, the Swift corrections are much   COMMENT  larger (~0.7 seconds at launch). At this writing (June 2005) the       COMMENT  spacecraft clock still lags behind reference clocks on the ground but  COMMENT  also runs fast.  The spacecraft clock is currently accelerating slowly.COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT  Time is divided into intervals, expressed in spacecraft MET.           COMMENT  Columns are: TSTART TSTOP TOFFSET C0 C1 C2 TYPE CHI_N DOF              COMMENT  where                                                                  COMMENT     TSTART and TSTOP are the interval boundaries (MET),                 COMMENT     TOFFSET is the clock offset (ie, TIMEZERO),                         COMMENT     MAXGAP is the largest gap with no data (-1 if unknown),             COMMENT     CHI_N is the reduced chi-square value (-1 if unknown),              COMMENT     DOF is the number of degrees of freedom,                            COMMENT     TYPE indicates the segment clock continuity (0=YES; 1=NO).          COMMENT  (MAXGAP, CHI_N, DOF, and TYPE are retained for continuity with         COMMENT  the file format used by RXTE but the values are currently all          COMMENT  defaults and are not used in computing the actual clock offset.        COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT  For a mission time of T, the correction in seconds is computed         COMMENT  with the following:                                                    COMMENT     T1 = (T-TSTART)/86400                                               COMMENT     TCORR = TOFFSET + (C0 + C1*T1 + C2*T1*T1)*1E-6                      HISTORY  Created with PUTCLOCKTAB                                               HISTORY  [originally written by C. Markwardt (UMD/GSFC) for RXTE                